{
 "model": "phase-2 fine-tune of unified_head9s.onnx (same architecture / IO / 133-d slices; the backbone unified_back9.onnx is unchanged and was frozen - the head trained on its features from the trace). Supervised fut1-3 / fut1f / def1-3 from phase-2 contacts (hp drop - 5 f, 卸势 ok at the 真气 step; def dodge only under a 金光 flare); combo / stage / ours / cont / land distilled from head9s; tell distilled with curtain (and non-dark 'dark') moved to none (phase two has no curtain). Use with args {\"phase\":2,\"head\":\"dufu/unified_head_p2.onnx\"}. Trainer: tools/dufu_train/train.py.",
 "io": {
  "inputs": [
   {
    "name": "seq",
    "shape": [
     1,
     30,
     207
    ],
    "dtype": "float32",
    "note": "the ONLY input: 30 steps oldest..current, each [192 backbone features | 15 aux], unchanged from v6. unified_head9s takes no image - the runtime must not capture / ROI-crop / resize a frame for the head any more (that was a deterministic no-op in unified_head9.onnx and cost ~15 ms per call)."
   }
  ],
  "output": {
   "name": "out",
   "shape": [
    1,
    133
   ],
   "dtype": "float32",
   "note": "v6 77 first (dufu.js reads offsets 0..76 unchanged), then the v8 slices; softmax per slice. Byte-identical to unified_head9.onnx's output for the same seq (the dropped image input provably never influenced it)."
  }
 },
